  "context_pill": "Section 44A: Trade Association Deficiency",
  "example_summary": "Boat Club, a trade association, seeks to set off its member expenditure deficiency of ₹ 1,85,000 against other income of ₹ 2,75,000 for AY 2026-27, subject to the 50% statutory ceiling.",
  "source_provision": "| Aspect | Statutory Rule | Tax Treatment |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Scope | Mutual Association (Trade Association) | Taxable as AOP/BOI |\n| Deficiency | Expenditure > Member Income | Set-off against other income |\n| Ceiling | Max deduction under Section 44A | 50% of Total Income (pre-deduction) |\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Section 44A Sequence\n1. Calculate deficiency: (Expenditure for members - Income from members).\n2. Set off against PGBP income first.\n3. If PGBP is insufficient, set off against other heads of income.\n4. Apply ceiling: Deduction cannot exceed 50% of the total income computed before this allowance.\n\n\n> [!WARNING] Statutory Trap\n- Any unabsorbed deficiency after the 50% ceiling cannot be carried forward to subsequent Assessment Years.\n- Section 44AA mandates strict maintenance of books of account to support such claims.",
